## Context: check the rendered evidence

The [original incident](/kb/incidents/4471/) says one issue and one queued fix,
but its rendered **What was merged** table shows two causes. That table is computed
by `CauseTable.svelte` from unique report IDs and the tenant-based `groupByCause`
logic, not from the incident prose or browser-locale intake labels.

This is a review of the export dated 2026-10-04, not a live support-system view.
The later engineering outcome is preserved separately below.

## Two problems, two tickets

The shared parser reads day-first input month-first; for example, R-41200 describes
7 April becoming 4 July. The booking-v3 hint is a separate mechanism: it says
`MM/DD/YYYY` while the form reads the tenant's day-first convention. A parser fix
does not establish that the hint was fixed.

<ReviewFindings />

## Received is not merged

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

Read `receivedAt` separately from `mergedAt`. The July merge peak records backlog
processing, not proof of a sudden arrival spike or an effective production fix.

## Decision: replace subject-only merging

**Proposed process change, not an accepted desk decision:** supersede
[accepted decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject/) with cause-based
deduplication. Preserve that accepted historical record unchanged.

Merge only when the established mechanism agrees, checking tenant locale,
booking-form version and channel. Identical subjects can hide different causes;
different subjects can describe the same cause. Browser locale and `intakeTag`
are clues, not substitutes for tenant configuration. Missing evidence means
investigate, not automatically merge.

The [old triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe/) repeats the subject-only policy, while its
rendered explorer demonstrates the distinction. Its old review date and staleness
warning are reasons to review the prose, not to rewrite an accepted decision.

<DedupeExplorer />

<EngineeringOutcomes />

## Consequences and follow-up

Keep both engineering records and their original counts. Separate parser
regressions from reports about the retired booking-v3 form. The five one-day
descriptions retain their supplied classification; their mechanisms are not
independently proven by this record's closure. Link this replacement rule from
operational guidance if approved by the desk owner.

